# mm.fs.native

A directory of the platform's own file system, mounted at a prefix: a test's
temporary directory, a tool's working tree, a host directory a program
shares. Linux serves it over the C++ standard library. A platform without a
file system of its own binds no provider, and a program reaching
mm.fs.native is unavailable there.

contain_symlinks, on by default, keeps the volume inside its root: a
symbolic link whose target lies outside the root is treated as absent. mm.fs
has already made ".." unable to climb out.

unmount detaches only volumes this module attached. The platform-interface
marker makes the provider part of an executable only when its closure
reaches mm.fs.native; with none bound the fallback answers Unsupported.
